speechtext:
I should like to get a
little information about this vote; I must confess I am ignorant in regard to it. How many months in the year do these boats operate that are giving the service from the mainland to those particular islands which my hon. friend (Mr. Caldwell) spoke about. He has figured that the population in one of these islands is small. Now, I presume these boats are simply carrying the passengers who live there backwards and forwards, delivering mail and so on. I should like to have particulars about the service that is carried on, and whether it would not be necessary to move the inhabitants off these islands to the mainland seeing that it requires so much in subsidies to maintain the services in question. My hon. friend (Mr. Caldwell) led me to believe that these islands were miniature islands. Well, there is lots of room on the mainland in the provinces of New Brunswick and Nova Scotia. Why do not these people leave these islands and settle there? It may be that some of these places are just summer resorts and the people frequenting them are getting the benefit of these services.
[Mr. Caldwell.}
